2.1 The following documents shall be considered an integral part of this Agreement:
• Attachment 1: Quotation No. [*], dated [*];
• Attachment 2: Bill of quantities, prices of materials and equipment, and labour (BOQ), dated [*];
• Attachment 3: Scope of Work.
2.2 In the event of any discrepancy or inconsistency between the provisions of this Agreement and any Attachment, the provisions of this Agreement shall prevail.
2.3 In the event of any discrepancy or inconsistency among the Attachments, the Contractor shall comply with the determination of the Owner, and such determination shall be final. The Contractor shall have no right to claim any additional Contract Price, damages or expenses from the Owner arising from such discrepancy or inconsistency.

14.1 The Contractor shall be deemed to be in breach of this Agreement if any of the following circumstances occurs or is reasonably certain to occur:
• the Contractor is unable to complete the Works within the stipulated period;
• the Contractor breaches any provision of this Agreement;
• it is reasonably certain that the Works will be defective or will otherwise be performed in breach of any provision of this Agreement;
• it is reasonably certain that the Contractor will be unable to complete the Works within the stipulated period;
• the Contractor becomes subject to an absolute receivership order or becomes bankrupt;
• the Contractor fails or refuses to comply with an instruction of the Owner’s acceptance committee; or
• the Contractor is wholly unable to continue performing the Works under this Agreement.
14.2 Upon the occurrence of a breach under clause 14.1, the Owner shall have the right to terminate this Agreement immediately and may engage a third party to perform the Works in place of the Contractor without prior notice. The Contractor shall be responsible for all costs and damages incurred by the Owner.
14.3 If the Contractor is in breach under clause 14.1 and the Owner has not exercised its right to terminate this Agreement, the Owner may, in addition to any other rights under this Agreement:
• continue the Works itself or engage a third party to continue the Works until completion, with the Contractor responsible for any additional costs;
• claim the costs of supervision where the Owner must supervise the Works itself or engage a third party to do so;
• withhold or deduct all amounts of the Contract Price that are due or will become due; and
• forfeit all or part of the retention and/or performance security provided by the Contractor under this Agreement, without prior notice, to cover costs, penalties and damages arising from the performance of this Agreement.
14.4 A Party shall not be deemed in breach where it is unable to perform its obligations due to force majeure.
14.5 Exercise of the right to terminate this Agreement shall not prejudice the Owner’s right to claim damages from the Contractor.
14.6 The Owner’s failure to exercise its termination right shall not release the Contractor from its obligations or liabilities under this Agreement. Neither Party shall be released from its obligations under this Agreement merely because of increased costs or other economic impacts arising from performance of its obligations.

15.1 Upon the Owner exercising its right to terminate this Agreement, the Owner may perform the Works itself or engage a third party to continue and complete the Works. The Owner shall have the following rights:
• the Owner or any person engaged to continue the Works may use construction tools and equipment, temporary works and construction materials that the Owner considers necessary to be retained for completion of the Works;
• the Owner may recover from the Contractor the costs of engaging a replacement contractor and the costs of materials and equipment required to complete the Works;
• the Owner may recover the costs of supervision incurred by the Owner in supervising the Works itself or engaging a third party to supervise the completion of the Works; and
• the Owner may withhold or deduct all amounts of the Contract Price that are due or will become due and forfeit all or part of the retention and/or performance security provided by the Contractor under this Agreement, without prior notice, to cover the costs, penalties and damages arising from the performance or completion of the Works.

16.1 Subject to the limitations set out in this Agreement, if a Force Majeure event prevents either Party from performing any obligation, in whole or in part, under this Agreement, the affected Party shall notify the other Party of the Force Majeure event and all relevant details as soon as reasonably practicable after its occurrence. The affected obligations shall be suspended or excused to the extent affected by the Force Majeure event.
16.2 “Force Majeure” means any event, condition or circumstance beyond the reasonable control of the Party claiming Force Majeure, without the fault or negligence of that Party, which causes delay or difficulty in performing any obligation under this Agreement, even if the affected Party has made reasonable efforts to prevent the event or mitigate its effects, including:
• lightning, storms, floods or unusually severe weather conditions;
• earthquake, landslide or other unforeseeable natural disaster relating to geography or land;
• protests, strikes or labour disputes;
• war (whether declared or not), invasion, terrorist acts, embargo, civil unrest, rebellion, panic, riot or sabotage by national enemies;
• land expropriation, compulsory seizure or intervention in the System, the Project site, any material property or rights of either Party, or any act, omission or failure by a government authority;
• any change in law or governmental action which prevents a Party from performing its obligations under this Agreement; or
• epidemic.
16.3 In the event of Force Majeure, the affected Party shall:
• immediately notify the other Party in writing of the Force Majeure event;
• have the right to temporarily suspend the affected obligations under this Agreement, only to the extent and for the period during which performance is prevented by the Force Majeure event;
• use reasonable efforts to remedy the relevant circumstances and resume performance as soon as practicable;
• report periodically to the other Party regarding the Force Majeure event and the measures taken to remedy it; and
• give written notice upon resumption of performance after the Force Majeure event ends.
16.4 If a Force Majeure event affects performance of this Agreement and continues for one hundred and eighty (180) consecutive days, either Party may terminate this Agreement without such termination constituting a default, provided that the affected Party can demonstrate that the Force Majeure event cannot be remedied within one hundred and eighty (180) days and continues to have an effect for more than three hundred and sixty-five (365) days.
